    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and all tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What I did\n\n**New `Tenure` helper** (`model/Tenure.java`) \u2014 a small single-responsibility unit that owns the membership tenure boundary, mirroring the existing `AgeBand`/`BusinessDay` helpers:\n- `daysAsOf(registrationDate, asOf)` \u2014 tenure in whole days\n- `qualifiesForTopLevel(registrationDate, asOf)` \u2014 encapsulates the *\"more than 365 days\"* rule (`QUALIFYING_DAYS = 365`)\n\n**`Owner.getMembershipLevel()`** \u2014 added tenure as the fourth level factor, following the same additive pattern already used for email and uniqueness, and raised the cap from 3 to 4:\n\n```java\nboolean tenured = this.registrationDate != null\n    && Tenure.qualifiesForTopLevel(this.registrationDate, LocalDate.now());\nif (tenured) { level++; }\nreturn Math.min(level, 4);\n```\n\nBecause reaching level 4 requires the tenure increment, and a newly created owner registers today (zero tenure), a new owner tops out at level 3 \u2014 exactly what the spec and the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test require. I updated the Javadoc to reflect the 1\u20134 range and the tenure gate.\n\nThe full suite is green.",
